(inside the binary distributions named above).


===============================================================================
ChordPro — behavior followed (The ChordPro Team)
===============================================================================

ChordSketch is a different program from ChordPro, with a different name, and
contains none of its source or data files. It follows the behavior, directive
names and configuration keys of ChordPro R6.100 and R6.101
(https://github.com/ChordPro/chordpro, Artistic License 2.0).
`crates/chordpro/src/chord.rs` reimplements in Rust the rule ChordPro uses
for spelling too-sharp keys as flats (`is_key_toosharp` in
`lib/ChordPro/Chords/Parser.pm`); no Perl code is copied.

The built-in chord voicings (guitar, ukulele, keyboard) were written for
ChordSketch, and the charango shapes are searched out from each chord's tones
at run time; none is taken from ChordPro (the common open-position chords
agree with ChordPro's because they are the standard shapes).


===============================================================================
ireal-reader and accompaniser — iReal Pro URL de-obfuscation and test data (MIT)
===============================================================================

`unscramble` and `obfusc50` in `crates/ireal/src/parser.rs`, which undo the
scrambling of an `irealb://` chart, are a Rust translation of `unscramble.js`
from pianosnake/ireal-reader (https://github.com/pianosnake/ireal-reader).
That routine follows `irealb_parser.lua` from ironss/accompaniser
(https://github.com/ironss/accompaniser). Several test URLs
(`crates/ireal/tests/fixtures/parser/`, the CLI tests, and the sample charts of
the playground and the iReal editor) are taken from the test corpus of
pianosnake/ireal-reader, some of them shortened or edited. The parser's
handling of the chart body follows the behavior of its `Parser.js`; the code is
ChordSketch's own.

Both projects are under the MIT License:

  - Copyright (c) Florin Alexandrescu (pianosnake/ireal-reader; the repository
    has no license file, its package.json names this author and MIT)
  - Copyright (C) 2013 Stephen Irons (ironss/accompaniser)

The MIT text, with the copyright lines above, is in
`crates/ireal/LICENSE-THIRD-PARTY.txt` (inside the `chordsketch-ireal` crate
package) and in `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md`.


